('h1', 'Introduction'),
('h2', 'Background'),
('p', 'University laboratories, makerspaces and teaching departments share a pool of high-value equipment such as cameras, oscilloscopes, VR headsets, 3D printers and laptops. Today these items are usually managed with spreadsheets, e-mail threads and paper sign-out sheets. Borrowers cannot see availability, approvers decide without context, custodians cannot tell who holds an overdue item, and faults reported at the desk are often lost before a technician sees them.'),
('p', 'The **Shared Equipment Reservation and Maintenance System (SERMS)** replaces this manual process with one web application that covers the full lifecycle of a shared asset: search and reservation, approval, checkout, return, overdue follow-up, fault reporting and repair. Every step is tracked, audited and visible to the right role.'),
('p', 'SERMS was built by Team 07 over four Sprints. All five core use cases and the administration, reporting and audit features are complete, merged to `main` and released through a gated GitHub Actions pipeline to https://serms.midas.cyou. In Sprint 4 the solution became a **scalable modular monolith**: stateless Spring Boot replicas sit behind an nginx load balancer and share one PostgreSQL 18 database, which also holds the HTTP sessions and scheduler locks. Releases are rolling updates with zero failed requests, and Prometheus and Grafana monitor every replica. This report describes that architecture from several viewpoints (context, logical, deployment, domain, data and detailed design), the DevOps lifecycle that delivers it, and how SERMS can evolve into microservices when load and team size justify it (Section 6).'),
('h2', 'Business Needs'),
('b', '**Fair, conflict-free access to scarce equipment.** Two borrowers must never hold the same item for overlapping time slots, even under concurrent requests (Proposal business rules 1 and 12).'),
('b', '**Accountability.** Every reservation, decision, checkout, return and repair is attributed to a user and kept in an append-only audit trail (rule 9).'),
('b', '**Faster turnaround.** Approvers see pending requests with context; custodians find the right reservation by asset tag or borrower name; reminders reduce overdue loans.'),
('b', '**Asset health.** A damaged return automatically opens a maintenance case and blocks new reservations until the item is repaired (rules 2, 7 and 8).'),
('b', '**Management insight.** Utilisation, overdue and maintenance reports support purchasing and staffing decisions.'),
('b', '**Operability at campus scale.** The system must serve at least 50 concurrent users within 2 seconds, survive the loss of one application instance and be released frequently without downtime.'),
