('h1', 'Quality Attributes'),
('h2', 'Performance'),
('p', '**Target:** 2 s response for 50 concurrent users; reports within 5 s (Proposal 7).'),
('b', '**Horizontal scaling:** stateless replicas behind `least_conn` load balancing; capacity grows linearly until the database becomes the bottleneck.'),
('b', '**Database tactics:** indexes on search, overlap and due-date columns; paginated list endpoints (`page`, `size`, `sort`); HikariCP pool of 10 per replica sized against PostgreSQL `max_connections`; JdbcTemplate for hot paths instead of ORM N+1 queries.'),
('b', '**Front-end tactics:** hashed static assets cached for one year (`immutable`), route-level code splitting (the Recharts report bundle loads only when opened), TanStack Query caching and 30 s polling instead of push.'),
('p', '**Evidence.** A k6 scenario (`scripts/load-k6.js`) runs virtual users that each log in, search and reserve a distinct item. Each run uses fresh borrowers and items; the table averages the measured runs, without warm-up runs. The host had 4 vCPU; in the 1 vCPU rows each replica was limited to one CPU, as if each had its own small host.'),
('tab', ['Scenario', 'Checks', 'p95 all', 'Login', 'Search', 'Reserve'], [
    ['50 users, 2 replicas, shared 4 vCPU (production setup)', '200/200 ×3', '1.21 s', '1.25 s', '0.22 s', '0.31 s'],
    ['50 users, 1 replica, shared 4 vCPU', '200/200 ×3', '0.96 s', '1.04 s', '0.13 s', '0.14 s'],
    ['50 users, 1 replica, 1 vCPU', '200/200 ×2', '4.09 s', '4.28 s', '0.82 s', '0.86 s'],
    ['50 users, 2 replicas, 1 vCPU each', '200/200 ×2', '2.05 s', '2.10 s', '0.36 s', '0.42 s'],
    ['150 users, 1 replica, 1 vCPU', '600/600 ×2', '10.33 s', '11.00 s', '3.86 s', '2.97 s'],
    ['150 users, 2 replicas, 1 vCPU each', '600/600 ×2', '5.47 s', '5.70 s', '1.43 s', '1.40 s'],
    ['150 users, 3 replicas, 1 vCPU each', '600/600 ×2', '3.87 s', '3.99 s', '0.65 s', '0.82 s'],
], [3400, 1200, 1100, 1100, 1100, 1100], 'k6 results (p95, no failed requests in any run)'),
('fig', '21-k6-scaling', 'p95 latency with 150 users as replicas are added (bars: all requests; orange: search; light blue: reserve)', {'max_h': 3.4}),
('p', 'With 50 users on the production setup, every operation meets the 2 s target. The earlier 2.26 s reserve p95, measured on a laptop with one instance, is not reproduced. When each replica has its own CPU, adding replicas roughly halves latency, which is the expected horizontal scaling. On one shared 4-vCPU host a second replica does not speed up 50 users, because both replicas compete for the same cores; there it adds availability. Sign-in is CPU-bound by design (BCrypt), so capacity should be sized for peak sign-in (AIS-03). Raw results are in `docs/evidence/scaling-20261104/`.'),
('h2', 'Availability'),
('b', '**Redundancy:** two app replicas by default. nginx moves a request to the next replica when a connect fails and replays a GET/HEAD it could not deliver. Measured: after one of two replicas was killed under continuous traffic, all 261 requests returned 200.'),
('b', '**Health checks:** Docker health checks on `/api/v1/health` (liveness and readiness probes are also enabled) and `pg_isready`; `restart: unless-stopped` restarts crashed containers.'),
('b', '**Zero-downtime release:** `scripts/rolling-update.sh` starts the new replicas, waits until they are healthy, then drains the old ones one at a time. Migrations are backward compatible. Measured: 0 failed signed-in requests in four rolling updates (Section 5.3).'),
('b', '**Recovery:** pre-release and daily `pg_dump` with 7-day retention, rehearsed restore into a scratch database (runbook-backup.md); RPO 24 h, RTO under 1 h.'),
('b', '**Monitoring:** Prometheus discovers each replica through Docker DNS. Alerts cover a replica down, fewer than two replicas, p95 above 2 s, 5xx above 2% and a waiting DB pool; the Grafana dashboard shows requests per replica.'),
('b', '**Known gaps:** single VM (AIS-01); a replica stopped outside Compose is not replaced automatically (AIS-07).'),
('h2', 'Security'),
('tab', ['Threat (STRIDE)', 'Control in SERMS'], [
    ['Spoofing', 'BCrypt password hashes; `JSESSIONID` cookie HttpOnly + Secure + SameSite=Lax; session-id rotation on login (also with Spring Session); `session_version` revocation; edge login rate limiting planned (AIS-09)'],
    ['Tampering', 'CSRF token (`XSRF-TOKEN` cookie + `X-XSRF-TOKEN` header), Bean Validation + Zod + database constraints, optimistic versions'],
    ['Repudiation', 'Append-only `audit_log` written in the business transaction'],
    ['Information disclosure', 'TLS and HSTS, CSP and security headers, ProblemDetail without stack traces, `/api/v1/prometheus` answered with 404 at nginx and scraped only on the internal network, no secrets in images'],
    ['Denial of service', 'Pagination limits, bounded retries, multiple replicas, 10 s upstream retry budget; edge `limit_req` planned (AIS-09)'],
    ['Elevation of privilege', '`@PreAuthorize` on every service method, no self-approval, admin-only role management with audit'],
], [2200, 6800], 'Security controls by STRIDE category'),
('p', 'DevSecOps controls run on every pull request: gitleaks (secrets), Trivy filesystem and image scans, Dependency Review, Dependabot security updates and CodeQL for Java and TypeScript. The OWASP ZAP baseline reported 0 FAIL / 5 WARN / 62 PASS against production (2026-10-17) and 0 FAIL / 2 WARN / 60 PASS against the local two-replica stack (2026-11-04).'),
('h2', 'Extensibility and Maintainability'),
('b', '**Modularity:** one module per bounded context with api/service/domain/repository layers; modules communicate through services, ports and events.'),
('b', '**Extension points:** new booking rules as `ReservationPolicy` strategies, new approval checks as chain handlers, new notification channels as `NotificationChannel` adapters, new event consumers as listeners.'),
('b', '**Contracts:** OpenAPI-generated client types and written contracts in `docs/contracts/`; changes need affected-owner confirmation.'),
('b', '**Testability:** injected `Clock`, port interfaces and Testcontainers make rules and races reproducible; 78% business-logic coverage with a 70% gate.'),
('b', '**Evolvability:** ownership of tables per context and stable domain events make extraction into services possible without rewriting business logic (Section 6).'),

