('h2', 'Source Control Strategy'),
('p', 'SERMS uses GitHub flow with short-lived branches. `main` is protected: changes arrive only through pull requests, the branch must be up to date with `main`, all 15 required checks must pass, and history is preserved with merge commits. Branch names state type and owner, for example `feat/<member>-<topic>` or `fix/<member>-<topic>`. Each PR follows the template (scope, linked issue, tests, evidence, affected owners), and team Done requires at least one member check in addition to green CI. Dependabot raises grouped security-update PRs.'),
