('h2', 'Continuous Delivery'),
('p', 'A push to `main` that changes application paths, or a manual dispatch, starts the `Deploy` workflow (Figure 19). The release gate refuses anything that is not the current `main` SHA with all 15 checks green and the `SERMS_PRODUCTION_READY` flag set. A human reviewer then approves the `production` environment. The deploy job connects over SSH with a pinned host key and runs `scripts/deploy.sh`:'),
('b', 'pre-release `pg_dump` backup;'),
('b', 'image build for the exact SHA;'),
('b', '`scripts/rolling-update.sh`: new replicas start next to the old ones and apply expand-only migrations; once all are healthy and nginx has seen them, the old replicas drain one at a time;'),
('b', 'web recreation and a health check through nginx.'),
('p', 'If a new replica is unhealthy, only the new replicas are removed and the previous release keeps serving. A later failure is rolled back by hand with the previous SHA images, which are kept. CI repeats the rolling update under signed-in traffic in `release-images` and fails on any non-200 response.'),
